Changes made in this pack (Apache License 2.0 section 4(b))
  prompt-orchestrator changed the files below on 2026-11-27. Each modified
  file carries a dated notice comment at its top. In SKILL.md, the comment
  follows the front matter.

  1. skills/playwright-cli/SKILL.md, front matter: added origin, vetting,
     vetted, license, upstream and upstream-commit. The name, the description
     and allowed-tools are unchanged.

  2. skills/playwright-cli/SKILL.md, the "## Installation" section: replaced the
     global install step `npm install -g @playwright/cli@latest` with one setup
     line per shell (bash or zsh, and PowerShell). The line puts the .bin folder
     of this pack's private npm prefix first on PATH and sets
     NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER=1, so the bare `playwright-cli` commands match the
     allowed-tools grant. The prefix path falls back to ~/.local/share when
     XDG_DATA_HOME is unset. The section names playwright-cli.cmd on Windows and
     asks the user before each install step. The npx local-version check above
     it is unchanged.

  3. skills/playwright-cli/references/pr-attachments.md: added the section
     "## Approval before posting". The agent drafts the pull request or issue
     text and the attachment first, then asks the user before running
     `gh pr create`, `gh pr comment`, `gh pr edit`, `gh issue create` or
     `gh issue comment`.

  4. skills/playwright-cli/references/test-generation.md: added a note after
     the upstream `npm init playwright@latest` code fence. The note says that
     the step installs packages, that the agent asks the user first and that
     the agent pins the version the user names. The code fence is unchanged.

  5. Em dashes removed from prose, with the facts kept and code fences left
     verbatim. Twenty prose em dashes were rewritten across four files:
     skills/playwright-cli/SKILL.md (1), references/session-management.md (1),
     references/test-generation.md (15) and references/video-recording.md (3).
     Three em dashes inside code fences stay verbatim: SKILL.md (2) and
     references/video-recording.md (1).

  The other reference files (element-attributes.md, playwright-tests.md,
  request-mocking.md, running-code.md, storage-state.md and tracing.md) are
  byte-identical to the upstream commit.
